{
  "abstract": "A Lean formalization of a technical lemma in the paper \"Nonlinear lower-tail large deviations at criticality\" by Matthew Kwan and Huy Tuan Pham. This lemma is used to solve a certain variational problem, which is necessary to characterise the probability that a random graph is triangle-free in the so-called \"critical regime\" where the edge probability is of order 1 / sqrt n.\nSpecifically, this lemma defines a \"certificate function\" G and proves that it satisfies a certain inequality. This involves lots of interval arithmetic.",
